# arXiv:2110.13338 — Nougat extraction stub

**Status:** STUB. Nougat OCR/math extraction was NOT run against this paper in
the original 2026-07-03 replication attempt. The paper was ingested via
`pdftotext -layout` into `work/paper.txt`, which was sufficient to locate the
noise recipe (ε=1 % two-qubit depolarising + T₁=50 µs, T_CNOT=200 ns) and the
Fig 3 CNOT-ladder circuit family used by the replication.

## Why this stub exists
The QC-100 backfill standard (2026-07-05 brief) requires an `extraction/nougat.mmd`
artifact per replication dir for downstream indexing/search. The numerical
replication did not depend on machine-readable versions of the paper's equations,
so no Nougat pass was performed at run time. This file marks that gap explicitly
rather than pretending it was done.

## When Nougat would matter here
The one place the replication would benefit from a proper Nougat extraction is
the quantitative check of Eqs. 10–11 (paper's per-shot variance formulae for
FIIM vs RIIM). The current replication reproduces the ordering those equations
predict (efficient recipe has lower per-shot variance than full recipe at
n_c=10) but does not compare the empirical variance against the algebraic
prediction. See `report/failure_analysis.md` §(b) for the open gap and
`report/open_questions.json` for the follow-up plan.

## How to fill this in later
```bash
cd ~/Dropbox/REPLICATE-PROJECT/QC-100/QC-2110.13338-efficient-zne-gate-error
# free endpoints only: uicgpu A100 idle time or Polaris PBS for larger batches
nougat --model 0.1.0-base work/paper.pdf --out extraction/
mv extraction/paper.mmd extraction/nougat.mmd
```

The resulting `.mmd` should contain Eqs. 1–14 (particularly 10 and 11) as
LaTeX-embedded math, which would let a future run compare the empirical
per-shot variances against the paper's algebraic predictions coefficient by
coefficient.

